WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.016 --> 00:00:19.599
3 Dear Daddy Longlegs, Almost two months have passed since I last wrote to you.

2
00:00:20.679 --> 00:00:24.541
That wasn't nice of me, but I haven't liked you very much this summer.

3
00:00:24.561 --> 00:00:26.802
(I'm just being honest!)

4
00:00:28.122 --> 00:00:33.032
I was so disappointed about not going to the McBrides' summerhouse.

5
00:00:33.052 --> 00:00:34.753
I don't understand why you wouldn't let me go.

6
00:00:36.334 --> 00:00:43.338
Here's how I wish our conversation had gone: Judy: "Please, sir, may I go to Sallie's house for

7
00:00:43.358 --> 00:00:43.758
the summer?

8
00:00:44.839 --> 00:00:46.580
It will be the best summer of my life."

9
00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:49.861
Daddy Longlegs: "Of course, my dear.

10
00:00:50.182 --> 00:00:51.082
Go have a good time.

11
00:00:52.083 --> 00:00:54.604
Meet lots of new people and learn lots of new things.

12
00:00:55.604 --> 00:00:57.085
Live outside in the fresh air.

13
00:00:58.326 --> 00:01:01.948
Rest and grow strong, so you'll be ready for another year of hard work."

14
00:01:04.128 --> 00:01:05.869
But we didn't have a conversation.

15
00:01:07.030 --> 00:01:08.471
You didn't even write me a letter.

16
00:01:08.491 --> 00:01:14.115
I only received a line from your secretary, ordering me to Lock Willow Farm.

17
00:01:15.536 --> 00:01:17.777
I hate how impersonal your commands are.

18
00:01:19.158 --> 00:01:20.419
That's what hurts my feelings.

19
00:01:22.340 --> 00:01:24.722
I'd like to receive a handwritten message from you.

20
00:01:25.863 --> 00:01:30.306
But instead I get those cold typewritten notes from your secretary.

21
00:01:31.667 --> 00:01:35.141
If you ever acted like you cared, I'd do anything for you.

22
00:01:36.681 --> 00:01:37.782
I know we had a deal.

23
00:01:39.502 --> 00:01:41.383
You promised to pay for my education.

24
00:01:43.324 --> 00:01:48.626
In return, I was to write nice long letters without expecting any response from you.

25
00:01:50.467 --> 00:01:51.727
You're keeping your promise.

26
00:01:53.128 --> 00:01:55.449
And I suppose you think I'm not keeping mine.

27
00:01:57.090 --> 00:01:59.210
But it's a hard bargain, Daddy Longlegs.

28
00:01:59.651 --> 00:02:00.531
It really is.

29
00:02:00.551 --> 00:02:02.912
I'm so lonely.

30
00:02:04.632 --> 00:02:07.814
When I was sick last year, you sent me a handwritten note.

31
00:02:09.755 --> 00:02:13.158
Now, when I'm feeling forgotten, I often reread your card.

32
00:02:14.499 --> 00:02:16.900
You're the only person I have to care about.

33
00:02:17.881 --> 00:02:19.722
And I really don't know anything about you.

34
00:02:21.283 --> 00:02:27.007
Here's what I truly want to say: Although my feelings are still hurt, I've decided to forgive you

35
00:02:27.267 --> 00:02:28.448
for sending me to the farm.

36
00:02:31.488 --> 00:02:35.310
But I still don't enjoy getting Sallie's letters about the fun they're having!

37
00:02:38.051 --> 00:02:39.071
So let's begin again.

38
00:02:41.352 --> 00:02:43.473
I've been writing and writing this summer.

39
00:02:45.514 --> 00:02:49.575
I've finished four short stories and sent them to four different magazines.

40
00:02:52.777 --> 00:02:56.678
I have a desk in the corner of the attic where Jervie used to play on rainy days.

41
00:02:58.459 --> 00:03:01.120
Speaking of rain it rained here for a week.

42
00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:05.721
But now the air is fresh and the sun is shining.

43
00:03:09.182 --> 00:03:13.963
If you're stuck in that hot, crowded New York City, I'd like to send you this bright, lovely

44
00:03:14.023 --> 00:03:25.786
day. Good afternoon, Judy August 10 Dear Daddy Longlegs, You'll never guess who's coming to Lock Willow!

45
00:03:26.766 --> 00:03:27.907
Jervis Pendleton!

46
00:03:29.627 --> 00:03:31.788
The mail is delivered once a day around noon.

47
00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:36.162
Mrs. Semple opened his letter right after lunch today.

48
00:03:37.323 --> 00:03:38.705
We were still sitting at the table.

49
00:03:38.725 --> 00:03:40.586
"Oh my!

50
00:03:40.986 --> 00:03:42.628
Jervie wants to visit us!"

51
00:03:43.068 --> 00:03:43.829
she exclaimed.

52
00:03:43.849 --> 00:03:47.112
"He hasn't been here for years."

53
00:03:47.132 --> 00:03:49.994
"So why is he coming now?"

54
00:03:50.414 --> 00:03:50.875
I asked.

55
00:03:52.176 --> 00:03:54.698
"He says he's tired and needs a break.

56
00:03:55.939 --> 00:03:58.621
He wants to rest on a nice, quiet farm."

57
00:03:58.641 --> 00:04:01.584
"How long is he staying?"

58
00:04:03.368 --> 00:04:04.930
Mrs. Semple read the letter again.

59
00:04:04.950 --> 00:04:06.931
"He doesn't say.

60
00:04:08.633 --> 00:04:11.315
Maybe he'll stay for a week or maybe two or three.

61
00:04:11.335 --> 00:04:14.418
He'll see how he feels when he gets here.

62
00:04:15.479 --> 00:04:16.900
But, oh my!

63
00:04:17.321 --> 00:04:19.943
We have so much cleaning to do before he arrives!"

64
00:04:21.284 --> 00:04:24.267
I glanced around the dining room and didn't see a speck of dirt.

65
00:04:24.287 --> 00:04:26.769
"What is there to clean?"

66
00:04:26.789 --> 00:04:29.532
"The whole house!

67
00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:34.122
We must clean it from top to bottom and wash all the curtains.

68
00:04:35.343 --> 00:04:36.944
I hope our neighbor is available.

69
00:04:38.164 --> 00:04:39.966
I want to hire her to wash the windows.

70
00:04:40.906 --> 00:04:43.528
And you must go into town for me this afternoon, Judy.

71
00:04:44.688 --> 00:04:48.791
We'll need two cans of brown paint for the stairs and back hall floor."

72
00:04:50.012 --> 00:04:52.433
I couldn't believe the change that had come over Mrs.

73
00:04:52.493 --> 00:04:57.276
Semple. She seemed almost frantic as she started a list for me.

74
00:04:58.996 --> 00:05:00.697
"How long do we have to do all this?"

75
00:05:01.237 --> 00:05:01.717
I asked.

76
00:05:03.298 --> 00:05:05.779
Mrs. Semple looked at the letter again and shook her head.

77
00:05:05.799 --> 00:05:08.240
"I have no idea.

78
00:05:09.140 --> 00:05:12.362
He doesn't say if he's arriving today—or in two weeks."

79
00:05:15.103 --> 00:05:20.865
August 11 I didn't get this letter mailed because I was so busy helping Mrs.

80
00:05:20.945 --> 00:05:26.688
Semple. There was no sign of Jervie yesterday.

81
00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:29.641
The house is now immaculate.

82
00:05:32.884 --> 00:05:34.105
I hope he arrives soon.

83
00:05:35.486 --> 00:05:37.667
Otherwise we'll have to clean all over again.

84
00:05:39.369 --> 00:05:42.331
I'm looking forward to having someone to talk to besides Mrs.

85
00:05:42.371 --> 00:05:46.494
Semple. She's nice, but she can be rather boring.

86
00:05:48.215 --> 00:05:50.917
All she ever talks about is what happens right here on the farm.

87
00:05:52.558 --> 00:05:54.400
I suppose I was like that at the orphanage.

88
00:05:55.628 --> 00:06:00.134
But at college I got used to having real conversations about a variety of things.

89
00:06:02.617 --> 00:06:04.179
So I'll be glad to see Jervie.

90
00:06:05.500 --> 00:06:08.263
I'll tell you all about his visit in my next letter.

91
00:06:09.685 --> 00:06:11.387
Yours always, Judy
